It seems the simplest approach to analyze trend from point counts is to=20=

estimate global estimates of density from a sample of points each year wi=
th=20
Distance and then to use a relatively simple linear or nonlinear model to=
=20
estimate trend across years.  If the same points are surveyed each year i=
s=20
it more appropriate to use auto regression or timeseries approaches that=20=

address temporal autocorrelation?  For more complicated mixed models that=
=20
might better address address temporal or spatial correlation, or even oth=
er=20
fixed effects that affect density, would you produce point level estimate=
s=20
of densites and then use the point level estimate to fit models?

